### Step 7: Edit the messages

Under **Messages**, every toast and label is editable. Leave a field blank to use the default. Some messages accept placeholders:

```
Compare limit reached         {max}
Add All to Cart: all added    {added}
Add All to Cart: some added   {added} and {skipped}
Add All to Cart: none added   {skipped}
```

You can also rename the **Wishlist** and **Compare** menu entries in My Account.

That’s it. Click **Save changes** and the settings apply immediately.

### JavaScript event

After every AJAX update, the extension triggers premmerce-filter-updated on the document, so you can rebind your scripts to the new products:

```
jQuery( document ).on( 'premmerce-filter-updated', function () {
	// Re-initialize your scripts for the new products.
} );
```

### Examples

Hide the filter on one category:

```
add_filter( 'premmerce_product_filter_active', function ( $active ) {
	if ( is_product_category( 'gift-cards' ) ) {
		return false;
	}
	return $active;
}, 20 );
```

Change the Filter button’s text:

```
add_filter( 'premmerce_filter_submit_button_label', function () {
	return __( 'Show products', 'your-textdomain' );
} );
```

Treat another plugin’s taxonomy as a brand, so it can be used on brand pages, in SEO rules, and in {brands}:

```
add_filter( 'premmerce_product_filter_brand_taxonomies', function ( $taxonomies ) {
	$taxonomies[] = 'my_brand_taxonomy';
	return $taxonomies;
} );
```

Keep one category’s rules out of sitemaps:

```
add_filter( 'premmerce_filter_seo_sitemap_rules', function ( $rules ) {
	return array_filter( $rules, function ( $rule ) {
		return 15 !== (int) $rule['term_id'];
	} );
} );
```

Stop redirecting old prefixed URLs after turning on “Don’t use an attribute prefix”:

```
add_filter( 'premmerce_filter_redirect_prefixed_urls', '__return_false' );
```

### PHP functions

```
premmerce_bundles_get_bundles_html( int $id ): string
```

Returns the HTML of the bundles whose main product is the product ID 
```
$id
```

, the same as 
```
[premmerce_get_bundles_by_main_product_id id="…"]
```

. It returns an empty string when the product has no bundles that can be bought, and always in wp-admin and admin-ajax.php requests, where the extension’s front end isn’t loaded. Category bundles and the bundles of a variable product’s variations aren’t included.

```
// Show the product's bundles straight after the add to cart form.
// Combine with the snippet in "Change where bundles are placed" so they don't also show in their usual place.
add_action( 'woocommerce_after_add_to_cart_form', function () {
	if ( function_exists( 'premmerce_bundles_get_bundles_html' ) ) {
		echo premmerce_bundles_get_bundles_html( get_the_ID() ); // Template output from the extension.
	}
} );
```

```
premmerce_bundles()->checkBundleInCart( int $bundle_id ): bool
```

Returns whether the bundle with that ID is in the current cart.

```
if ( function_exists( 'premmerce_bundles' ) && premmerce_bundles()->checkBundleInCart( 12 ) ) {
	// Bundle 12 is in the cart.
}
```

### Filters

```
premmerce_bundles_hide_product_from_self
```

| Argument | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| $hide | bool | false by default. Return true to stop bundles being output. |

The filter runs once for each bundle as it renders, everywhere bundles show. It has no other arguments, so use conditional tags to decide. When it returns 
```
true
```

, the section’s title still prints.

```
// Don't show bundles on products in the Clearance category.
add_filter( 'premmerce_bundles_hide_product_from_self', function ( $hide ) {
	if ( is_product() && has_term( 'clearance', 'product_cat', get_the_ID() ) ) {
		return true;
	}
	return $hide;
} );
```

### Actions

```
premmerce_bundles_admin_page_tab_content
```

| Argument | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| $tab_slug | string | The open tab on Premmerce > Frequently Bought Together: product-bundles or category-bundles |

Fires where the open tab’s content is output on the bundles admin page. The extension uses it to render the tab, so your callback’s output appears after it.

```
add_action( 'premmerce_bundles_admin_page_tab_content', function ( $tab_slug ) {
	if ( 'category-bundles' === $tab_slug ) {
		echo '<p>' . esc_html__( 'Category bundles show on products assigned directly to the category.', 'your-text-domain' ) . '</p>';
	}
}, 20 );
```

### Change where bundles are placed

The extension adds its placement hooks on 
```
wp
```

, from the **Bundle position** setting. To place bundles yourself, remove them after that and output them with the shortcode or 
```
premmerce_bundles_get_bundles_html()
```

. The object is the extension’s internal front-end class, so check it exists:

```
add_action( 'wp', function () {
	$fbt = isset( $GLOBALS['premmerce_bundles_frontend'] ) ? $GLOBALS['premmerce_bundles_frontend'] : null;
	if ( ! $fbt ) {
		return;
	}
	// "Before product description" (classic and block themes).
	remove_action( 'woocommerce_after_single_product_summary', array( $fbt, 'renderProductBundles' ), 1 );
	remove_filter( 'render_block', array( $fbt, 'prependProductBundles' ), 9 );
	// "After product description".
	remove_action( 'woocommerce_after_single_product_summary', array( $fbt, 'renderProductBundles' ), 12 );
}, 20 );
```

