## Inspect and cancel the retry

Save the following PHP as 
```
cancel-retry.php
```

 where you run WP-CLI. It runs in preview mode unless you explicitly add 
```
apply
```

. Replace 
```
123
```

 in the commands with the renewal order ID.

```
<?php
/**
 * Inspect or cancel the latest pending retry for one renewal order.
 * Run with WP-CLI: wp eval-file cancel-retry.php ORDER_ID [apply]
 */

if ( empty( $args[0] ) || ! ctype_digit( (string) $args[0] ) ) {
	throw new RuntimeException( 'Pass a numeric renewal order ID.' );
}

$order_id = (int) $args[0];
$apply   = isset( $args[1] ) && 'apply' === $args[1];
$order   = wc_get_order( $order_id );

if ( ! $order || ! wcs_order_contains_renewal( $order ) ) {
	throw new RuntimeException( 'The ID must belong to a renewal order.' );
}

if ( ! WCS_Retry_Manager::is_retry_enabled() || false === has_action( 'woocommerce_subscriptions_retry_status_updated', 'WCS_Retry_Manager::maybe_delete_payment_retry_date' ) ) {
	throw new RuntimeException( 'The retry cleanup hooks are not active.' );
}

$subscriptions = wcs_get_subscriptions_for_renewal_order( $order );

ion( 'The retry cleanup hooks are not active.' );
}

