## Developer: exclude orders from syncing

If you need to keep certain orders out of Xero entirely — for example, orders for products that you invoice through a different system — you can do this in code with the 
```
wc_xero_should_sync_order
```

 filter. It applies to automatic sync and to the manual **Send to Xero as Invoice** action, so excluded orders never reach Xero.

Return 
```
false
```

 to skip an order. The filter receives the order being synced, so you can decide based on products, customer, order total, or any other order data. This example keeps every order that contains one of the listed product IDs out of Xero:

```
add_filter( 'wc_xero_should_sync_order', function ( $should_sync, $order ) {
    $excluded_product_ids = array( 123, 124, 125, 126, 127, 128, 129 );

    foreach ( $order->get_items() as $item ) {
        if ( in_array( $item->get_product_id(), $excluded_product_ids, true ) ) {
            return false;
        }
    }

    return $should_sync;
}, 10, 2 );
```

There is also a 
```
wc_xero_should_sync_payment
```

 filter, which controls payment creation only. Return 
```
false
```

 to record the invoice in Xero but skip the payment.

