### 3.4. How to Set Different Price Suffixes (Incl. / Excl. VAT) for B2B / B2C

If you use the plugin’s tax exemption feature, and a user is VAT exempt, **some themes will automatically set** an incl. VAT / excl. VAT suffix.
However, if your theme does not, here’s how you can configure this with a code snippet.
**The code below sets “excl. VAT” for b2b users and “incl. VAT” for b2c users as suffixes**:

```
// get if user is b2b
$user_is_b2b = get_user_meta(get_current_user_id(),'b2bwhs_b2buser', true);

if ($user_is_b2b === 'yes'){
    add_filter( 'woocommerce_get_price_suffix', 'add_price_suffix', 99, 4 );

    function add_price_suffix( $html, $product, $price, $qty ){
        $html = '<small class="woocommerce-price-suffix"> excl. VAT</small>';
        return $html;
    }
} else {
    add_filter( 'woocommerce_get_price_suffix', 'add_price_suffixtwo', 99, 4 );

    function add_price_suffixtwo( $html, $product, $price, $qty ){
        $html = '<small class="woocommerce-price-suffix"> incl. VAT</small>';
        return $html;
    }
}
```

To use the snippet above, you can add it to your functions.php file or to a Snippets plugin.

